  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "aufi7WQNiiZBrfQRckbkWYFHGYg=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:50.974Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Critical TechWorks' row records one vertical, automotive, with the researcher's own emphasis on \"only\", and a tool field of \"n/a\". Everything else is the standard carry-over: a provisional v2 tail entry, rescored mechanically on size and slot occupancy, never scored on v3.\n\nA single vertical constrains what could be built with the firm. Any demo would be tied to one sector's processes and would carry no reuse into the rest of the pipeline, which is a real cost when the point of a demo is to be shown twice. With no platform record, the slot-occupancy half of the rescore had nothing to work on, so the tier rests on scale and vertical narrowness.\n\nThe flag nonetheless still asks for an OSS-portfolio screen before acting, which makes this exclusion provisional in the same breath as it is stated \u2014 the same pattern as the other do-not-pitch rows carried over from v2.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Critical TechWorks (PT)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> DERIVED, NOT SCORED ON v3 \u2014 v2 row rescored mechanically (size + slot-occupancy only). Run the OSS-portfolio screen before acting. v2 verticals: Automotive only",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:50.974278Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:50.974282Z"
    }
  },
